{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ellipseIn","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rect","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Rect3D","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSpatial6Rect3DV"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"name":"rect","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The rectangle that bounds the ellipse."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is a convenience function that creates a path of an ellipse.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Using this convenience function is more efficient than creating a path and adding an ellipse to it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The ellipse is approximated by a sequence of Bézier curves."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Its center is the midpoint of the rectangle defined by the rect parameter."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If the rectangle is square, then the ellipse is circular with a radius equal to one-half the width (or height) of the rectangle."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If the rect parameter specifies a rectangular shape, then the major and minor axes of the ellipse are defined by the width and height of the rectangle."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ellipse forms a complete subpath of the path—that is, the ellipse drawing starts with a move-to operation and ends with a close-subpath operation, with all moves oriented in the clockwise direction.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"If you supply an affine transform, then the constructed Bézier curves that define the ellipse are transformed before they are added to the path.","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Initializer","symbolKind":"init","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI4PathV9ellipseInAC0A7Spatial6Rect3DV_tcfc","title":"init(ellipseIn:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ellipseIn","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Rect3D","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSpatial6Rect3DV"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Path"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a path as an ellipse within the given rectangle."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Path\/init(ellipseIn:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/path\/init(ellipsein:)"]}],"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"OpenSwiftUI"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Path":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Path","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/path","title":"Path","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The outline of a 2D shape."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Path"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Path"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Path/init(ellipseIn:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/path\/init(ellipsein:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifie